    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n76690" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παίονες</span></b> , οἱ,
			<u>Paeonians</u>, a people of Macedonia, <i><span class="en">
			Il.
			2.848
		</span></i>, etc.; <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παίων στρατός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					540
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.): <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παιονία</span></b> , 
				Ion.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιη,</span>
			ἡ, <i>their land</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				17.350
			</span></i>, etc.:—Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παιονικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ἔθνη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					2.96
				</span></i>
			, etc.; pecul. fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παιονίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.33
			</span></i>.—In late writers used for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παννονία, Παννόνιοι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VS</u>
				2.1.12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				49.36
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hippiatr.</u>
				124
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ</span></div>
